    "session": "HttpOnly cookie holding the Google-signed ID token, re-verified on each use"
  },
  "note": "All decoding, processing and WAV encoding happen in the browser with Web Audio API and OfflineAudioContext. Practice setups are saved in browser localStorage only and never uploaded; ZIP packs are assembled locally. Server endpoints create Waffo checkout sessions, verify signed payment webhooks, verify Google ID tokens and look up completed orders; they never receive audio files. Google sign-in is lazy: the GIS script, the auth cookie and all auth requests are absent until a visitor buys Pro or requests a Pro feature. Pro is a soft unlock verified against a real Waffo order, not DRM: because all processing is local, a determined user could modify the page script.",
